    "created_at": "2026-11-20T08:17:09Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-20T08:17:09Z",
    "body": "The File API side of this is underway: [w3c/FileAPI#222: Fold File and Directory Entries API into File API](https://github.com/w3c/FileAPI/pull/222) merges the Entries API text into the File API spec. The HTML-bound parts were deliberately left out of that PR. Listing them here so the split is tracked:\n\n- The [HTML: Forms](https://wicg.github.io/entries-api/#html-forms) section: form integration, including extending the entry list construction steps to set `File/webkitRelativePath`.\n- The [HTML: Drag and drop](https://wicg.github.io/entries-api/#html-data) section: `DataTransferItem.webkitGetAsEntry()`.\n- The `webkitdirectory` attribute on `input`, which HTML currently does not document at all. The File API spec links to it, so the reference stays dead until HTML defines it.\n- The `webkitEntries` population behavior, which the attribute's documentation must capture: it is only populated for drag-and-drop, not picker selections, and with `webkitdirectory` it stays empty, the directory structure being reconstructed from `files` and `webkitRelativePath`.\n\nRelated open issues on the WICG repo:\n\n- [WICG/entries-api#12: Should \"change\" fire if files does not change, only webkitEntries?](https://github.com/WICG/entries-api/issues/12)\n- [WICG/entries-api#15: Should .webkitEntries be populated for dialog selections?](https://github.com/WICG/entries-api/issues/15)\n- [WICG/entries-api#24: Behavior if both webkitdirectory and multiple attributes are specified](https://github.com/WICG/entries-api/issues/24)\n- [WICG/entries-api#28: Behavior if both webkitdirectory and accept attributes are specified](https://github.com/WICG/entries-api/issues/28)\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
